{
  "status": "investigation-only",
  "date": "2026-09-14",
  "scope": "Inspect all ten October 11 frames, compare published models at matching epochs, and identify the native image behind the published October 11 view. No camera correction or photographic surface prepared.",
  "findings": [
    "The prominent lower-right crater-like structure persists in both cameras at all five exposures. This visual sequence check does not establish its catalogue identity or planetocentric centre.",
    "Among all ten native frames, 05:08:49 Camera 2 best matches the corresponding Vernazza Figure B.2 photographic panel: fit correlation 0.998325, withheld correlation 0.998630. Camera 1 at the same time gives 0.980083 and 0.990882. The two held-out interior quadrants were not used in the four-parameter image fit; comparing candidate images still makes these selection evidence, not an untouched final validation set.",
    "The best Camera 2 image-to-paper fit rotates by -0.03125 degrees. It does not support an extra ~2-degree rotation of the released photograph. Rotations for the other observation times vary through the burst, as expected for the rotating body.",
    "Our frozen model views resemble published broad topography at three matching epochs. Published pole-marker axes differ by 1.44–2.41 degrees. The Marsset October 11 ADAM comparison has interior correlation 0.916 after 2D silhouette centroid/area normalization. These image statistics are not native-pixel camera-error bounds.",
    "The initial diagnostic used Lambert shading. ADAM Calculate_AO.c defines mu0/(mu+mu0)+0.1*mu0. Using that source-backed law improves correlation with Vernazza OASIS panels from 0.40–0.65 to 0.86–0.90, without changing the frozen cameras. OASIS rendering settings are not reproduced exactly; this is a sensitivity comparison, not a photometric calibration.",
    "The four old tentative named-crater picks remain unresolved. Their residuals cannot be used as absolute camera errors, and neither the burst nor the published-model comparison qualifies a new photographic surface."
  ],
  "nextDiscriminatingCheck": "Use the identified 05:08:49 Camera 2 / Figure B.2 pairing to resolve the remaining image-to-model pose and interior correspondence. Do not rotate or warp the photograph to make uncertain crater names agree; retain the pole-marker discrepancy until its convention or precision is explained.",
